Reading something else that mentioned rings of conflict, another idea
crossed my mind - make the utility of the ring go down as the
adventurer's level goes up. A ring of conflict is a life saver for a low
level character aswarm in orcs or killer bees, but it is _way_ too
powerful for a very high level character, who ought to be able to get by
on a reputation and a charming personality by then. Still, it wouldn't
be fair (or fun) to make the ring entirely useless somewhere in midgame,
either.

So how about the chance per turn of a monster attacking another monster
instead of attacking or approaching the character wearing a ring of
conflict be modified from 1 to ( 30.0 - adventurer's_level ) / 30.0;
translated into random() calls.

This would make the ring increasingly less powerful, while still useful,
and remove one form of game abuse that seems generally accepted as in
need of repair. Also the degradation in the utility of the ring would be
gradual enough that no obvious point at which to stop using it would
exist until the highest level.

If you want the ring to always be at least a little useful, change the
30.0's to 40.0's.

Comments?

